   "title": "Disk usage critical on production Attribution Engine nodes (ANZ region)",
   "description": "We are seeing a critical disk usage alert on our production instances of the Attribution Engine in the ANZ region. The alert fired around 08:00 UTC today. Currently, we have about 37 users attempting to run reports, but they are experiencing timeouts or failures likely due to the lack of space. The disk usage is consistently hitting 98-99% despite our normal retention policies. Could you please advise if there is a cleanup job that failed or if we need to expand the storage volume?"
  },
  {
   "i": 13306,
   "title": "Payment Gateway issues in sandbox",
   "description": "There seem to be some problems with the sandbox payment gateway. Users are complaining about overcharges and subscriptions not renewing correctly. Also, the currency conversion looks wrong. Please check."
  },
  {
   "i": 13307,
   "title": "Critical: Cache Service connection refused in LATAM production",
   "description": "We are facing a major outage with the Cache Service in our LATAM production environment. Since 14:00 local time, all applications are throwing 'connection refused' errors when trying to hit the cache cluster. This is impacting over 12,000 users immediately. We have traced this back to a recent update on the client libraries and we are 100% sure this is a version incompatibility issue between the new SDK and the current cache cluster configuration. The previous version worked perfectly until we rolled out the update yesterday. Please prioritize fixing the compatibility gap."
  },
  {
   "i": 13308,
   "title": "Webhooks failing with HTTP 429 on Payment Gateway v2 (EU-Central)",
   "description": "Since approximately 10:00 AM CET, our production environment in EU-Central has been experiencing issues with webhooks not firing from the Payment Gateway v2. Instead of successful delivery, we are receiving a significant volume of HTTP 429 (Too Many Requests) errors. This has prevented order fulfillment for about 324 users. We have checked our endpoint and it is healthy, so the throttling seems to be originating from your side. We need this resolved urgently to prevent further revenue loss."
  },
  {
   "i": 13309,
   "title": "Security Alert: Elevated Privileges and Certificate Warnings in Webhook Engine (US-West)",
   "description": "Our security team has flagged two critical issues with the Webhook Engine in our US-West production cluster. First, we are observing elevated privileges being granted to service accounts that should be restricted, which poses a significant security risk. Second, multiple internal services are throwing certificate warnings when communicating with the webhook endpoints, suggesting a potential misconfiguration in the TLS stack. These issues are affecting 6,417 users and require immediate investigation to rule out a compromise or configuration drift."
  },
  {
   "i": 13310,
   "title": "Bulk import partial failure and stuck provisioning in SSO Module",
   "description": "We attempted a bulk user import via the SSO Integration Module this morning. The process appears to have partially failed. Specifically, the provisioning status is stuck in 'Pending' for a subset of records, and we have noticed that duplicate accounts were created for several users who were already in the directory. No users are currently reporting impacts, but we need to clean up the duplicates and ensure the remaining imports complete successfully."
  },
  {
   "i": 13311,
   "title": "Permission Engine API returning empty responses and malformed JSON",
   "description": "We are encountering issues with the Permission Engine. Our clients are reporting that the webhook integrations are not firing correctly. When we manually test the API endpoints, we are receiving HTTP 200 responses but with malformed JSON bodies, and in many cases, the response body is completely empty. This is blocking about 142 users from accessing the dashboard. The team believes the Permission Engine service itself is misconfigured."
  },
  {
   "i": 13312,
   "title": "Compliance reports incomplete and audit logs missing entries in Payment Gateway",
   "description": "We have identified discrepancies in our compliance documentation generated by the Payment Gateway v2 in the EU-Central production environment. Several required compliance reports are coming out incomplete, and when we cross-reference with the audit logs, we find that specific transaction entries are missing. This is impacting our ability to certify transactions for 438 active users and poses a risk for our upcoming regulatory audit. Please investigate the data consistency between the reporting module and the audit trail."
  },
  {
   "i": 13313,
   "title": "UI elements misaligned in Notification Hub staging environment",
   "description": "During our QA review of the Notification Hub in the staging environment (LATAM), we found that several UI elements are misaligned, particularly in the campaign configuration panel. This is a visual bug but it is causing significant friction for our internal testers and stakeholders, impacting about 470 users who are reviewing the new features. It appears the CSS for the modal dialog is overlapping with the header. This needs to be fixed before we can proceed with the user acceptance testing sign-off."
  },
  {
   "i": 13314,
   "title": "HTTP 403 errors when accessing Invoice Service",
   "description": "We are receiving HTTP 403 Forbidden errors when trying to access certain endpoints within the Invoice Service in the production LATAM region. This started occurring unexpectedly. Currently, no users are reporting issues, but our monitoring has picked up the increase in 403s. We need to understand why the access is being denied to ensure it doesn't escalate into a user-facing problem."
  },
  {
   "i": 13315,
   "title": "Overcharging in staging Payment Gateway",
   "description": "Some of our test accounts in the staging environment for Payment Gateway v2 are showing overcharges. It's happening randomly. Please check why this is occurring as it affects our testing of about 30 users."
  },
  {
   "i": 13316,
   "title": "Password reset links expiring prematurely in SSO Module (US-East)",
   "description": "Users in our US-East production environment are reporting that password reset emails sent by the SSO Integration Module contain links that expire almost immediately. By the time they click, the link is invalid. This is affecting approximately 48 users who are currently locked out of their accounts. The standard validity period should be 1 hour, but it seems to be much shorter or the token validation is failing. This is causing a moderate impact on user productivity and support ticket volume."
  },
  {
   "i": 13317,
   "title": "Audit log missing entries in Analytics Dashboard staging (ANZ)",
   "description": "We are noticing gaps in the audit logs within the Analytics Dashboard in our ANZ staging environment. Certain actions performed by our test users are not appearing in the history log. This makes it difficult for our security team to verify changes during the testing phase, impacting about 57 users. We need to ensure that all actions are properly logged before moving to production to maintain compliance."
  },
  {
   "i": 13318,
   "title": "Certificate expiry warning and elevated privileges in Billing Disputes Handler",
   "description": "Our internal security scan for the Billing Disputes Handler in the ANZ staging environment flagged two issues. First, there is a warning that the SSL certificate is approaching expiration (or is already invalid in some contexts). Second, we observed that a service account has elevated privileges that exceed the required role definition. This affects only 2 internal users currently, but we need to address these configuration drifts to ensure the environment is secure and ready for deployment."
  },
  {
   "i": 13319,
   "title": "Missing audit log entries and certificate warnings in Wallet Service",
   "description": "In our EU-Central production environment, the Wallet Service is exhibiting two concerning behaviors. We have identified that certain transaction types are not generating audit log entries, resulting in missing records. Additionally, some of our microservices are receiving certificate warnings when connecting to the Wallet API. This is affecting approximately 18 users who rely on full transaction visibility and creates a potential security concern. Please investigate both the logging mechanism and the certificate trust chain."
  }
